# ⭐ Ubuntu Commands (Your Laptop)

## **Identify storage devices**
```
lsblk
```

## **Unmount SD card partitions**
```
sudo umount /dev/mmcblk0p1
sudo umount /dev/mmcblk0p2
sudo umount /media/hans/bootfs
sudo umount /media/hans/rootfs
```

## **Check if anything is using the SD card**
```
sudo lsof | grep mmcblk0
```

## **Check read‑only status**
```
lsblk -o NAME,RO
```

## **Fix read‑only flag (if needed)**
```
sudo hdparm -r0 /dev/mmcblk0
```

## **Move OS image to /tmp**
```
mv 2024-07-04-raspios-bookworm-arm64.img.xz /tmp/
cd /tmp
```

## **Extract the OS image**
```
unxz 2024-07-04-raspios-bookworm-arm64.img.xz
```

## **Flash Raspberry Pi OS**
```
sudo dd if=/tmp/2024-07-04-raspios-bookworm-arm64.img of=/dev/mmcblk0 bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync
```

## **Eject SD card**
```
sudo eject /dev/mmcblk0
```

## **Fix SSH “host key changed” error**
```
ssh-keygen -f "/home/hans/.ssh/known_hosts" -R "192.168.1.22"
```

## **SSH into the Pi**
```
ssh hans@192.168.1.22
```

## **Scan network (if needed)**
```
sudo nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24
```

## **Ping the Pi**
```
ping 192.168.1.22
```

## **Open camera stream in VLC**
```
vlc tcp/h264://192.168.1.22:8888
```

