# ⭐ Raspberry Pi Commands (On the Pi via SSH)

## **Check Pi IP**
```
hostname -I
```

## **Enable SSH (if needed)**
```
sudo raspi-config
```

## **Test camera preview**
```
rpicam-hello
```

## **Take a photo**
```
rpicam-still -o image.jpg
```

## **Record a 10‑second video**
```
rpicam-vid -t 10000 -o video.h264
```

## **Record video with audio**
```
rpicam-vid -t 10000 --audio -o video.mp4
```

## **Start live network stream (H.264)**
```
rpicam-vid -t 0 --inline --listen -o tcp://0.0.0.0:8888
```

## **Check if stream is listening**
```
sudo ss -tulpn | grep 8888
```

## **Install MJPEG streamer (browser‑friendly)**
```
sudo apt install mjpg-streamer
```

## **Start MJPEG stream**
```
mjpg_streamer -i "input_uvc.so" -o "output_http.so -w /usr/share/mjpg-streamer/www -p 8080"
```

